0..74 Comment "// Copy-on-write: a copy of a long string shares its buffer and counts one"
75..151 Comment "// more holder, and a write copies the buffer only when another string holds"
152..229 Comment "// it; a buffer held once is written in place. A short string\'s bytes are its"
230..304 Comment "// own, so its copy is a copy of at most the inline capacity. Either way a"
305..375 Comment "// write to one string is never seen through another (Racordon et al.,"
376..454 Comment "// \"Implementation strategies for mutable value semantics\", _Journal of Object"
455..519 Comment "// Technology_ 21(2), 2022, doi:10.5381/jot.2022.21.2.a2, § 3)."
521..584 Comment "// The lists; the byte lists; the owned bytes; where they live."
